WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.680
Everyone likes Paul Rudd.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.680
He might be the perfect movie star, he leads
a hit Marvel franchise, yet he seems down

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.700
to earth.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.820
He broke through in the classic '90s teen
comedy Clueless before becoming one of the

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.550
comedy cool kids with Wet Hot American Summer
and Anchorman before segueing into superhero

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:16.460
mode as Ant-Man.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.440
Rudd likes to laugh and keep it light, so
it's no surprise that he generates a lot of

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:20.940
bloopers.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.160
And to offer hilarious proof, we've taken
a deep dive to bring you some of the funniest

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.260
moments from behind the scenes of his biggest
movies.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.260
Just some kid stuff

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.780
What makes little kids freak out, in a good
way, more than anything else?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.640
Being present for stuff they think they're
not supposed to see.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.540
For example, bad words.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.010
They've been told their entire lives that
some words must never be said, so it only

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:48.260
stands to reason that when they actually hear
one, they become enthusiastically amused,

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.760
like in this outtake from Ant-Man

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.300
"Cuff that ass----!"

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:53.920
"Got it."

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.820
"I heard you!"

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.900
"I heard you!"

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.000
Why, robot?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.380
Judd Apatow likes to keep things loose and
collaborative on his sets, and since Paul

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:09.250
Rudd has an agile comic mind, he's wound up
in a few of Apatow's movies, including The

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.180
40-Year-Old Virgin.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.600
His character works alongside Steve Carell's
at a big box electronics store, which gives

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.520
the actors plenty of opportunity to play with
goofy gadgets.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.500
In this not-quite-appropriate-for-the-final-cut
sequence, Rudd interrupts a conversation to

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.940
show off a cool robot toy.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.560
"Check it out, man, new robo-sapiens!"

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.640
Black market panther

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.800
In Anchorman, a movie full of hilarious sequences,
one of the best occurs when ace 1970s San

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.070
Diego reporter and self-proclaimed ladies'
man Brian Fantana shows off his stash of intoxicating

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.520
colognes to Ron Burgundy.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.460
The prize of his collection: Sex Panther.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.280
"They've done studies, you know.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.580
60% of the time, it works every time."

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.540
"That doesn't make sense."

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.880
In this outtake, the elaborate, panther-shaped
mechanical prop doesn't work at all.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.920
"... fell off.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.800
It's cost me $13,000, it really pisses me
off."

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.020
Knocking a few back to the future

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.900
Pretending to be intoxicated, improvising
lines, and doing either of those things while

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.680
a co-star is angrily yelling into your ear
can't be easy, but Rudd manages all three

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.420
of those tasks in this unused scene from Knocked
Up.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.740
While his character gets progressively more
drunk in a restaurant, he slurs and stumbles

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.740
through some Back to the Future-themed goofing.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.740
'I'm gonna, you know what, I'm gonna build
you a skateboard and see what you do in the

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.740
town square."

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:38.960
"Stop talking."

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.820
"You guys are gonna love it in the future,
trust me."

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.940
"And then I'm gonna go…"

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.080
"Stop it!"

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.480
"I'm gonna go to the Twins Oaks mall.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.000
That use to be the… Hill Valley!"

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.180
Cracking up is only natural

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.140
The 2012 comedy Wanderlust concerns a big-city
couple so sick of urban annoyances that they

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.920
decide to try life on a nature-positive, free-love,
hippie-style commune.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.040
In this outtake, Paul Rudd tries to convince
Jennifer Aniston that they need to give up

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.040
the natural life.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.160
"Really, I don't think we're supposed to be
in a place."

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.760
"Many apologies, Mr. Baldwin."

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.880
Role-ing right along

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:23.720
In the 2008 comedy Role Models, Paul Rudd
and Seann William Scott play a couple of guys

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.400
forced into community service.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.280
All that stress highlights the differences
between the two, resulting in a fight, which

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.520
created a few unusable outtakes.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.960
"This coming from a guy who likes girls a
whole bunch."

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.480
When to call cut

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:47.720
In 2010, Rudd starred opposite Reese Witherspoon
in How Do You Know, where he plays a nice

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.960
guy named George who gets caught up in a federal
investigation of his father's company.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.040
He also finds time to fall in love.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.820
George is more than a bit nervous, and judging
by this blooper, those traits seeped into

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.320
Rudd's psyche.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:04.500
"I'm gonna tell you exactly what I like, everything
I have inside.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:06.220
Kiss kiss?

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.140
Nuts to you!"

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:10.000
What a schmuck

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.540
Dinner for Schmucks is an odd comedy about
odd people.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:17.760
It stars Rudd as a guy caught up with a strange
club that requires guests to bring an oddball

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.360
along to regular dinner parties.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.900
His candidate is a weirdo named Barry, played
by Steve Carell.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.040
While shooting one particular scene, things
got slightly weirder than expected.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.680
"I was just microwaving some Hot Pockets."

